  "function": "Butyrate production from dietary fiber",
  "description": "ButyraCult-5 is a 5-strain synthetic consortium designed to convert complex plant polysaccharides into butyrate. It combines primary degraders (cellulose/hemicellulose hydrolysis), intermediate fermenters (acetate/ lactate producers) and terminal butyrogens that channel reducing equivalents into butyryl-CoA. Cross-feeding of acetate and lactate between members stabilizes butyrate yields under pH fluctuation.",
